# Build context = the assembled workspace root (see app/Dockerfile header).
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` rebuilds node_modules inside the image and the generator produces all
# generated artifacts, so nothing host-side under here is needed in the context.
# Everything excluded below is gitignored locally and pure transfer/cache bloat;
# shipping it forces the daemon to copy ~1.2GB and busts COPY-layer caches on
# every build (the 64MB host binary + 50MB of local DBs change constantly).

# Dependency trees — ~1.1GB at root alone. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` recreates the whole
# workspace link graph from package-lock.json inside the image.
**/node_modules

# Per-member git repos (each sibling is its own clone). The build never reads
# git history; drive/.git alone is ~4MB.
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# Local PocketBase databases — never wanted in the image. The runtime creates a
# fresh /app/pb_data (Dockerfile `mkdir`) and operators bind-mount over it.
**/pb_data
**/pb_test_data

# Stray host-compiled binary (Mach-O arm64, 64MB) left in the server tree from
# local `go build`. The go-builder stage produces the real Linux binary; this
# one is dead weight and would never run in the image anyway.
app/server/app

# Build/tooling caches and transient outputs (all gitignored, all regenerated).
**/dist
**/build
**/.expo
**/.vite
**/.vite-temp
**/tmp
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache
**/.worktrees

# ...but the vendored PocketBase fork's admin UI is a CHECKED-IN build output,
# not a regenerable one: ui/embed.go does `//go:embed all:dist`, so the Go
# compiler needs those files present or every stage building the fork fails with
# "pattern all:dist: no matching files found". The `**/dist` rule above would
# strip it from the context, so re-include it (later patterns win).
!tinycld/third_party/pocketbase/ui/dist

# Editor / OS cruft.
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.superpowers

# Local secrets — must never enter the image.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pem
google-play-service-account.json

# Docs / meta that the build doesn't consume (kept small, but no reason to ship).
CUTOVER.md
README.md
**/CONTRIBUTING.md
**/LICENSE
